@startuml
!include ../../../../images/common-sequence.iuml

title MQTT — Firmware Update

box "On-Premises" $OnPrem
    participant "Client" as client
    participant "MQTT Broker" as mqtt
    participant "Home Assistant" as ha
end box

box "AWS" $AWS
    participant "FireFly-Cloud" as cloud
end box

== Auto Discovery ==

client -> mqtt : **Publish Auto Discovery** retained\nhomeassistant/update/FireFly-{UUID}-update/config\n""JSON payload""
mqtt -> ha : **Publish Auto Discovery**\nhomeassistant/update/FireFly-{UUID}-update/config
ha -> ha : **Create firmware update entity**\n(initially Unavailable)
client -> mqtt : **Subscribe**\nFireFly/{UUID}/update/set

== OTA Check ==

client -> client : **OTA check interval elapsed**
client -> cloud : **Check for new OTA firmware**\nGET /ota/client/{product_hex}?current_version=...

alt 200 OK — update available
    cloud --> client : **200 OK**\n""JSON payload""
    client -> mqtt : **Publish firmware update state** retained\nFireFly/{UUID}/update/state\n""JSON payload""
    mqtt -> ha : **Publish firmware update state**\nFireFly/{UUID}/update/state
    ha -> ha : **Set Firmware Update Entity**\n""Update Available""
else No update or unavailable
    cloud --x client : Unavailable or non-200 Response
end

== Install ==

ha -> mqtt : **Publish install command**\nFireFly/{UUID}/update/set\n""do-update""
mqtt -> client : **Publish install command**\nFireFly/{UUID}/update/set\n""do-update""
client -> cloud : **Download firmware**
client -> client : **Apply OTA update and restart**

@enduml
